Packaged from the official GitHub release nupkg (Squirrel app package), not a
from-source build: XIVLauncher's main csproj targets net9.0-windows + WPF and
there is no supported Linux publish for this tag; the "native Linux" line is a
separate upstream project (XIVLauncher.Core / Flathub) with its own version
stream. The Windows build runs cleanly under our Wine 11.14 (new WoW64, no
lib32) -- DXVK/Vkd3d-Proton are installed as deps so the FFXIV game client can
use them once launched.

Layout: lib/xivlauncher holds the whole lib/app tree from the nupkg; the
bin/xivlauncher wrapper prefers Wine-Lutris-GE for daemons/FFXIV compatibility
then falls back to Wine, and boots a dedicated prefix if absent. Because the
app is self-contained, no .NET framework install in the prefix is required.

Icon: the nupkg's setup.ico is converted to a 256px PNG (ImageMagick) at build
time for the desktop entry.